//  v4: one of three interchangeable aes_sbox backends (see aes_sbox.sv's
//  header comment and aes_sbox_pkg.sv). This one is the minimum-area,
//  minimum-read-port option: a single logical 512x8 ROM (0x000-0x0ff
//  forward, 0x100-0x1ff inverse -- see rtl/aes_sbox_512.mem, generated by
//  scripts/gen_aes_sbox_mem.py from the same FIPS-197 table this module's
//  content is descended from) read one byte at a time, so a 32-bit word
//  substitution takes 4 cycles. Reference: the table values themselves are
//  unmodified from secworks/aes (see https://github.com/secworks/aesaes);
//  everything else here (the ROM, the byte-serial controller, the req/rsp
//  handshake) is new for v4.

